<section id="bbs011" image-layout="blank"><card-template-instructions>Image plus text split: a working title and a short paragraph on the left, one framed photograph on the right in a padded surface plate that keeps the theme's corner radius.</card-template-instructions><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item colspan="35" vertical-align="center" id="V90KURIEyB"><h2>The second delivery day changed the week</h2><p>Regional accounts that took two deliveries a week ordered smaller quantities more often, held less stock, and stopped calling about shortages. Drivers finished routes earlier because each stop carried fewer pallets.</p><p>The change cost one additional van and paid for itself within the quarter.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="25" padding="0" id="Sm4qYKd9eF"><img meta="{&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}" alt="Documentary photograph of a delivery van being loaded at a small regional depot in early morning light, stacked boxes on a hand truck, no readable text or logos" image-style="plain-photo" background="true" source="image.ai-generated" saved-media-id="fa2j8duuf6833b9" src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/gammatemplatelibrary/g_hdwa21xzz00ppa2/template-assets/d35f1ddcf4a5572ea042646dbf4f935e/786oL3DPf0uKu1MJ84oot.jpg"></grid-item></grid></section>